{
  "bookId": "PSA",
  "chapter": 91,
  "bookEnglish": "Psalms",
  "bookChineseSimplified": "诗篇",
  "bookChineseTraditional": "詩篇",
  "verses": [
    {
      "verse": "1",
      "en": {
        "text": "He who dwells in the secret place of the Most High will rest in the shadow of the Almighty.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "住在至高者隐密处的，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "住在至高者隱密處的，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "2",
      "en": {
        "text": "I will say of the LORD, “He is my refuge and my fortress; my God, in whom I trust.”",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "我要论到耶和华说：",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "我要論到耶和華說：",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "3",
      "en": {
        "text": "For he will deliver you from the snare of the fowler, and from the deadly pestilence.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "他必救你脱离捕鸟人的网罗",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "他必救你脫離捕鳥人的網羅",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "4",
      "en": {
        "text": "He will cover you with his feathers. Under his wings you will take refuge. His faithfulness is your shield and rampart.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "他必用自己的翎毛遮蔽你；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "他必用自己的翎毛遮蔽你；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "5",
      "en": {
        "text": "You shall not be afraid of the terror by night, nor of the arrow that flies by day,",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "你必不怕黑夜的惊骇，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "你必不怕黑夜的驚駭，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "6",
      "en": {
        "text": "nor of the pestilence that walks in darkness, the destruction that wastes at noonday.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "也不怕黑夜行的瘟疫，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "也不怕黑夜行的瘟疫，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "7",
      "en": {
        "text": "A thousand may fall at your side, and ten thousand at your right hand; but it will not come near you.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "虽有千人仆倒在你旁边，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "雖有千人仆倒在你旁邊，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "8",
      "en": {
        "text": "You will only look with your eyes, and see the recompense of the wicked.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "你惟亲眼观看，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "你惟親眼觀看，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "9",
      "en": {
        "text": "Because you have made the LORD your refuge, and the Most High your dwelling place,",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "耶和华是我的避难所；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "耶和華是我的避難所；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "10",
      "en": {
        "text": "no evil shall happen to you, neither shall any plague come near your dwelling.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "祸患必不临到你，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "禍患必不臨到你，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "11",
      "en": {
        "text": "For he will put his angels in charge of you, to guard you in all your ways.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "因他要为你吩咐他的使者，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "因他要為你吩咐他的使者，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "12",
      "en": {
        "text": "They will bear you up in their hands, so that you won’t dash your foot against a stone.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "他们要用手托着你，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "他們要用手托着你，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "13",
      "en": {
        "text": "You will tread on the lion and cobra. You will trample the young lion and the serpent underfoot.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "你要踹在狮子和虺蛇的身上，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "你要踹在獅子和虺蛇的身上，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "14",
      "en": {
        "text": "“Because he has set his love on me, therefore I will deliver him. I will set him on high, because he has known my name.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "神：因为他专心爱我，我就要搭救他；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "上帝：因為他專心愛我，我就要搭救他；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "15",
      "en": {
        "text": "He will call on me, and I will answer him. I will be with him in trouble. I will deliver him, and honor him.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "他若求告我，我就应允他；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "他若求告我，我就應允他；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "16",
      "en": {
        "text": "I will satisfy him with long life, and show him my salvation.”",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "我要使他足享长寿，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "我要使他足享長壽，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    }
  ]
}